{"duration": 65.811, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "Robert Maillart walked across his own bridges to test them.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.109}, {"beat": 0, "text": "He rarely tested a bridge before construction.", "start": 3.329, "end": 5.685}, {"beat": 0, "text": "He checked the finished bridge by crossing it himself.", "start": 5.905, "end": 8.284}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Before 1900, engineers used shapes that were easy to analyze with mathematics.", "start": 8.704, "end": 13.412}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Maillart preferred common sense to predict how a full-size bridge would behave.", "start": 13.632, "end": 17.746}, {"beat": 1, "text": "His designs went beyond the common boundaries of concrete design.", "start": 17.966, "end": 21.68}, {"beat": 2, "text": "So Maillart combined the road deck with the arch ribs.", "start": 22.1, "end": 24.883}, {"beat": 2, "text": "That created one closely integrated structure of very thin concrete.", "start": 25.103, "end": 28.957}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, Maillart's hollow arch was like a cardboard box: light in your hands, yet hard to twist.", "start": 29.377, "end": 34.622}, {"beat": 4, "text": "A box has multiple walls, so it resists twisting better than an I-beam.", "start": 35.042, "end": 38.749}, {"beat": 4, "text": "At the same height, a box carries more load than an I-beam.", "start": 38.969, "end": 41.927}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Concrete carried compression, which means squeezing.", "start": 42.147, "end": 44.584}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Steel bars carried tension, which means pulling.", "start": 44.804, "end": 47.213}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Maillart used the material efficiently.", "start": 47.633, "end": 49.696}, {"beat": 5, "text": "His Salginatobel proposal won a competition partly for its low cost.", "start": 49.916, "end": 54.307}, {"beat": 6, "text": "In 2001, a British trade journal voted Salginatobel 'the most beautiful bridge of the century.'", "start": 54.727, "end": 60.669}, {"beat": 6, "text": "And Maillart checked his work the hard way: by crossing the bridge himself.", "start": 60.889, "end": 64.691}], "words": [{"w": "Robert", "start": 0.17, "end": 0.495, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Maillart", "start": 0.545, "end": 1.17, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "walked", "start": 1.27, "end": 1.52, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "across", "start": 1.545, "end": 1.82, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "his", "start": 1.845, "end": 1.92, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "own", "start": 1.945, "end": 2.095, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "bridges", "start": 2.145, "end": 2.52, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "to", "start": 2.57, "end": 2.62, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "test", "start": 2.67, "end": 2.895, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "them.", "start": 2.92, "end": 3.152, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "He", "start": 3.395, "end": 3.495, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "rarely", "start": 3.545, "end": 3.87, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "tested", "start": 3.92, "end": 4.245, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "a", "start": 4.295, "end": 4.32, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "bridge", "start": 4.395, "end": 4.745, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "before", "start": 4.795, "end": 5.02, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "construction.", "start": 5.07, "end": 5.761, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "He", "start": 5.991, "end": 6.066, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "checked", "start": 6.116, "end": 6.366, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "the", "start": 6.391, "end": 6.441, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "finished", "start": 6.491, "end": 6.766, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "bridge", "start": 6.816, "end": 7.166, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "by", "start": 7.216, "end": 7.316, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "crossing", "start": 7.366, "end": 7.716, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "it", "start": 7.741, "end": 7.791, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "himself.", "start": 7.816, "end": 8.379, "line": 2, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Before", "start": 8.748, "end": 8.998, "line": 3, "beat": 1}, {"w": "1900,", "start": 9.048, "end": 1